{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","title":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":855,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-3-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","line":2458,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[minimizing curve is a geodesic]\n  \\label{cor:dc-ch3-3-9}\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch3-3-6, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length, def:dc-ch3-3-1, def:dc-ch3-2-1}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.9}\n  If a piecewise differentiable curve $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$, parametrized\n  proportionally to arc length, has length $\\le$ that of any other piecewise\n  differentiable curve joining $\\gamma(a)$ to $\\gamma(b)$, then $\\gamma$ is a\n  geodesic; in particular it is regular.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  For $t\\in[a,b]$ let $W$ be a totally normal neighborhood of $\\gamma(t)$\n  and $I\\subset[a,b]$ a closed interval with $t\\in I$ and $\\gamma(I)\\subset W$.\n  Then $\\gamma_I$ joins two points of a normal ball; by the hypothesis and\n  \\cref{prop:dc-ch3-3-6}, $\\ell(\\gamma_I)$ equals the length of the radial geodesic joining\n  them, so $\\gamma_I$ coincides with that geodesic. As $\\gamma_I$ is parametrized\n  proportionally to arc length it is a geodesic on $I$, hence at $t$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[minimizing curve is a geodesic] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a64632d6368332d332d39\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23prop%3Adc-ch3-3-6\">↗ prop:dc-ch3-3-6</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-9-localization\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-9-corner\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-9-anchored\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-chart-length\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-3-1\">↗ def:dc-ch3-3-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch3-2-1</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.9</span></span>If a piecewise differentiable curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$</span>, parametrized proportionally to arc length, has length <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\le $\">$\\le $</span> that of any other piecewise differentiable curve joining <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (a)$\">$\\gamma (a)$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (b)$\">$\\gamma (b)$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> is a geodesic; in particular it is regular.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\in [a,b]$\">$t\\in [a,b]$</span> let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> be a totally normal neighborhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t)$\">$\\gamma (t)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I\\subset [a,b]$\">$I\\subset [a,b]$</span> a closed interval with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\in I$\">$t\\in I$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (I)\\subset W$\">$\\gamma (I)\\subset W$</span>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _I$\">$\\gamma _I$</span> joins two points of a normal ball; by the hypothesis and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23prop%3Adc-ch3-3-6\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d332d36\">item 2</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\ell (\\gamma _I)$\">$\\ell (\\gamma _I)$</span> equals the length of the radial geodesic joining them, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _I$\">$\\gamma _I$</span> coincides with that geodesic. As <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma _I$\">$\\gamma _I$</span> is parametrized proportionally to arc length it is a geodesic on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$I$\">$I$</span>, hence at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t$\">$t$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#ex:dc-ch3-3-10","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6","title":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6","label":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-3-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-3-1","label":"def:dc-ch3-3-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch3-2-1"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#ex:dc-ch3-3-10","title":"ex:dc-ch3-3-10","label":"ex:dc-ch3-3-10"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#thm:dc-ch7-2-8","title":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8","label":"thm:dc-ch7-2-8"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","title":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[minimizing curve is a geodesic]\n  \\label{cor:dc-ch3-3-9}\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch3-3-6, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner, lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length, def:dc-ch3-3-1, def:dc-ch3-2-1}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.9}\n  If a piecewise differentiable curve $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$, parametrized\n  proportionally to arc length, has length $\\le$ that of any other piecewise\n  differentiable curve joining $\\gamma(a)$ to $\\gamma(b)$, then $\\gamma$ is a\n  geodesic; in particular it is regular.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  For $t\\in[a,b]$ let $W$ be a totally normal neighborhood of $\\gamma(t)$\n  and $I\\subset[a,b]$ a closed interval with $t\\in I$ and $\\gamma(I)\\subset W$.\n  Then $\\gamma_I$ joins two points of a normal ball; by the hypothesis and\n  \\cref{prop:dc-ch3-3-6}, $\\ell(\\gamma_I)$ equals the length of the radial geodesic joining\n  them, so $\\gamma_I$ coincides with that geodesic. As $\\gamma_I$ is parametrized\n  proportionally to arc length it is a geodesic on $I$, hence at $t$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6","title":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-localization","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-corner","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-9-anchored","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-3-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-3-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch3-2-1","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}